GRAMMAR.md §8 `@files`, API.md N2, DECISIONS 277: a template variable names `id` (the key) or a field of the entry; `{nope}` names neither and is the checker's unknown-name finding at the variable, with the nearest name in scope (`id` or a field) as its hint; the let holding it is broken, and nothing else is reported.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Row {
  name: String
}

@files("{nope}/{nmae}/{id}.canon")
local let rows: table Row = {
  first { name: "x" }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2102]  a/a.canon:7:10
  unknown name nope (did you mean name?)

error[E2102]  a/a.canon:7:17
  unknown name nmae (did you mean name?)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
